WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
Elephant and Castle, south London.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:07.140
Here stood the Heygate
estate: 1,212 homes,

3
00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.610
1,020 of them owned by the council.

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.710
The estate was knocked down.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.270
A new scheme, approved in January
2013, has 3,000 new homes.

6
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.110
Nearly half of the new
development is public space,

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.610
including one of central
London's largest new parks.

8
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.290
But who is the new city for?

9
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.930
The people who lived there before?

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.850
In this mission, you'll meet the
building blocks of a new kind of city,

11
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.830
from fortress spaces to edge cities.

12
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.410
Then you'll go from Belfast's old
shipyards to the edge of Washington,

13
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.330
DC, to test each idea.

14
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.110
Your mission: decide who
the new city is really for.
